<article class="env-lemma" id="0GNQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GNQ">Lemma <span data-tag="0GNQ">56.2.6</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be an additive category with arbitrary direct sums and cokernels. There is an equivalence of categories between </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the category of functors $F : \text{Mod}_ A \to \mathcal{B}$ which are right exact and commute with arbitrary direct sums, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the category of pairs $(K, \kappa )$ where $K \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{B})$ and $\kappa : A \to \text{End}_\mathcal {B}(K)$ is a ring homomorphism 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> given by the rule sending $F$ to $F(A)$ with its natural $A$-action. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GNN" data-tag="0GNN">56.2.5</a> and <a href="/tag/0GNL" data-tag="0GNL">56.2.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>